    "result": "Done! I've fixed both failing tests in the frai-core suite. Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n### 1. Governance test failure (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)\n**Problem**: The test imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` at the top level in `src/finetune/index.js` (while keeping them in the default export for backward compatibility).\n\n### 2. Eval test failure (`src/eval/index.test.js`)\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function signature was `(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging innocent text.\n\n**Fix**: Changed the `toxicityMetric` signature to `(outputs, references)` where the `references` parameter is accepted (for interface consistency with other metrics) but ignored. The function always uses the `defaultBannedTerms`.\n\nAll 28 tests now pass across 8 test files, and the complete repo builds successfully with no regressions.",
